            {
              "problem": "The components includes in SAP system is application layer, presentation layer and database layer where the application layer provides the interaction between user and UI and the presentation layer where the user interacts.",
              "fix": "State: \"SAP consists of three layers: the presentation layer (user interface), the application layer (business logic), and the database layer (data storage).\""
            },
            {
              "problem": "The application layer provides the application where the user will interact with the SAP GUI, where the presentation layer provides the SAP GUI to the user, where the database layer stores the information or helps the user to retrieve and store the data on the databases.",
              "fix": "Clarify: \"In the application layer, the system processes requests; the presentation layer displays the SAP GUI; the database layer stores and retrieves data.\""
            }
          ],
          "better_examples": [
            {
              "text": "SAP is structured into three layers: the presentation layer delivers the GUI, the application layer handles business logic, and the database layer manages data storage.",
              "why": "Clear, concise, and each layer\u2019s role is distinct."
            },
            {
              "text": "When a user logs in through the SAP GUI (presentation layer), the application layer authenticates the request and pulls data from the database layer.",
