          "model_answer": "Sure, let me walk you through that. I was the technical lead on a two\u2011person squad tasked with building a payment\u2011retry system for our e\u2011commerce platform. What I did was first map out the failure scenarios we were seeing \u2013 mainly network timeouts and insufficient funds \u2013 and then designed a lightweight, idempotent service that could queue failed transactions and automatically retry them up to three times with exponential back\u2011off. I split the work: my teammate focused on the API layer while I handled the retry logic and the integration tests. The key thing here is that we shipped the whole thing in six weeks, and after rollout we saw a 22% reduction in abandoned carts due to payment failures. It was a tight timeline, but the close collaboration and clear ownership helped us deliver on schedule and impact the bottom line.",
